<title>USA: PHLX sees SEC approval on flex options by year-end.</title>
<headline>PHLX sees SEC approval on flex options by year-end.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philadelphia Stock Exchange said Tuesday it expects the Securities and Exchange Commission by year's end will approve its plan to list flex options on stocks and indices.</p>
<p>Trading in the options would begin soon after SEC approval, probably in January, the exchange said.</p>
<p>Flex -- short for flexible exchange -- options allow users to tailor contracts to fit their specific needs.</p>
<p>The options will be available on 12 stocks including Abbott Laboratories Inc, Bank of Boston Corp and Dell Computer Corp.  </p>
<p>The other stocks are Federal National Mortgage Association (Fannie Mae), Georgia-Pacific Corp, Home Depot Inc, NationsBank Corp, Newmont Mining Corp, Placer Dome Inc, Quaker Oats Co, Time Warner Inc and WMX Technologies Inc.</p>
<p>Flex options will also be available on the PHLX/Keefe Bruyette &amp; Woods bank sector index, the gold/silver sector index, the national over-the-counter index, the semiconductor sector index, the Value Line composite index and the utility sector index.  </p>
<p>Flex options are currently available on select stocks and indices on the Chicago Board Options Exchange, American Stock Exchange and Pacific Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>--Derivatives desk, (312) 408-8750</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
